.TH pull 1  "pull " 
.SH NAME
pull \- Pull a cloud snippet into the local library
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpull\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-registry\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIREFERENCE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pull a cloud snippet into the local library
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Pull every tracked snippet plus remote\-only ones
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be pulled; change nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<AS_NAME>\fR
Save under a different local name
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
Pull a specific version instead of the latest
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite an existing local snippet without asking
.TP
\fB\-\-registry\fR \fI<REGISTRY>\fR
Registry base URL (default: `FORGEHUB_REGISTRY` or config)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIREFERENCE\fR]
`owner/name`, or a bare name for your own snippet. Required unless \-\-all is given
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fg pull alice/deploy
  fg pull ubuntu\-setup \-\-force
